description:
The two cleanup workflows were easy to confuse: one removes Connect preview bundles, the other gh-pages docs previews. Renames them `connect-previews-cleanup.yml` and `docs-previews-cleanup.yml` and gives every workflow a descriptive display name (several used their filename).

`py-release.yaml` keeps its filename: PyPI's OIDC publisher config names it.

@simonpcouch tagging you as an FYI. This shouldn't have any impact other than renaming the actions, but I added prefixes to all the actions to make it easier to keep them straight. If you hate it, let me know and we can switch to something else.

This PR adds a temporary workaround for slow apt downloads on the Linux R jobs, which point at `azure.archive.ubuntu.com` and have been stalling `setup-r` for 20 minutes or more. Each R workflow now switches apt to `archive.ubuntu.com` before `setup-r`, and gets a time limit so a stalled install fails quickly: 15 minutes for R CMD check (30 for R-devel, which compiles every dependency when its cache is cold) and 10 for the pkgdown and browser jobs.

This whole PR is meant to be reverted once the Azure mirror recovers. That is tracked in [posit-dev/commons#477](https://github.com/posit-dev/commons/issues/477).

@simonpcouch FYI on this. Doesn't change anything in practice, but gets rid of the slow Azure mirrors for now and runs the apt install in 45s instead of 20+ minutes like I was seeing yesterday and today.
